questions[605]{question_id,session_id,proposition,context,high_action,low_action,origin,info_gain,action_impact,novelty,adversariality,relevance,explore_exploit,resolution_rule,resolution_horizon,resolution_status,outcome,resolution_evidence,generated_at}:
  q-2026-10-02-001,2026-10-02-sample,Will spending two hours this week prototyping the smallest proof-agent experiment be higher-value than reading two more papers on it?,A recent open-source release makes small theorem-proving agents cheap to run locally.,prototype the experiment this week,keep reading first,news,82,90,70,65,88,exploit,Resolved true if a later note or repository shows the prototype ran and was judged more useful than the reading.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T08:00:00Z"
  q-2026-10-02-002,2026-10-02-sample,Should I stop project X before investing another ten hours in it?,The last three notes on X record no measurable progress.,stop X and write down why,continue X for ten more hours,notes,75,85,40,92,80,exploit,Resolved true if X is stopped within the horizon and no later note regrets it.,2026-11-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T08:00:00Z"
  q-2026-10-02-003,2026-10-02-sample,Am I continuing the site refactor because of sunk cost rather than expected future value?,Repository activity shows refactor commits but no new readers' features in a month.,freeze the refactor,finish the refactor,project,70,72,55,88,76,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note states the reason explicitly.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T08:00:00Z"
  q-2026-10-02-004,2026-10-02-sample,Will the result I rated 80% last session still look right after this month's new evidence?,Two later notes partly contradict it.,keep the belief,write a note revising it,calibration,60,45,35,70,66,exploit,Resolved by the next session's answer to the same latent variable.,next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T08:00:00Z"
  q-2026-10-02-005,2026-10-02-sample,Is a small immediate experiment better than more reading whenever my uncertainty is mainly empirical?,"",default to experiments first,keep deciding case by case,synthesis,66,58,62,50,70,explore,"Unresolved until several later records show experiments outperforming reading, or not.",2027-04-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T08:00:00Z"
  cal-20261002-030,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is running many parallel crewmates producing more learning for me than one carefully reviewed agent would?,50 commits on 1 Oct; my notes ask what should remain stronger after automation.,cap parallel crewmates at two for a week,keep scaling the fleet,synthesis,85,85,80,92,90,exploit,Resolved by a later note comparing a capped week with an uncapped week on notes written and decisions made; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-23,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-001,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Will at least half of the visualisations ported to the site this week still look worth porting if I ask in a month?,"156 site commits in seven days, 77 of them visualisation features; notes commits fell to zero.",pause porting and pick the 3 that matter,keep porting at this pace,synthesis,85,85,80,85,92,exploit,Resolved by the answer to a re-asked version of this question in a session after 2026-11-02; unresolved if not re-asked.,2026-11-02,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-008,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is merging the PR that marks 27 todos resolved without answers hiding exploration debt rather than paying it?,My own note says open investigations have no linked outcome records.,keep only todos with a written outcome resolved; reopen the rest as dropped,merge the PR as is,synthesis,85,80,85,92,90,exploit,Resolved true if PR 122 is merged unchanged and none of its 27 items gains an outcome note by 2026-11-30; false if outcomes or explicit 'dropped' reasons are recorded.,2026-11-30,resolved,false,"Items closed by https://github.com/yujieteo/site/pull/122 gained outcomes: the grilling compaction amendment (https://github.com/yujieteo/skills/pull/14) and the Mac agent-workstation skill (https://github.com/yujieteo/skills/pull/15), recorded in the 2026-10-02 closing note of data/notes.md (https://github.com/yujieteo/site/commit/066c279231a2144d4b0719b6a77561b95bc7103e).","2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-011,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Will using my wildcard before the Gameweek 6 deadline beat holding it to Gameweek 7 or later?,Over half of polled managers plan a GW6 wildcard; fixture swings outside Fulham are limited.,wildcard for Gameweek 6,hold the wildcard,news,80,92,70,75,90,exploit,Resolved by a later note comparing my Gameweek 6–8 points against the template; unresolved if not recorded.,2026-10-25,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-002,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Should I stop porting visualisations into standalone repositories for the next two weeks?,30 port commits since 26 Sep; most mirror repositories have 0 stars.,freeze new standalone repos for two weeks,keep the repository-first workflow,project,78,88,75,90,88,exploit,"Resolved true if no new yujieteo repository mirroring a visualisation is created between 2026-10-03 and 2026-10-16, false otherwise.",2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-023,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Should I enter the VR October Challenge on 3–4 October rather than keep studying Reg M-C?,"A Reg M-C online tournament runs this weekend; my notes are study, not play.",register and play it,keep studying,news,80,88,85,85,82,explore,Resolved true if a note or public result records my participation in the VR October Challenge.,2026-10-05,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-003,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Am I producing visualisations faster than I can personally use or learn from them?,55 catalogue records; the last notes from using one are the 30 Sep beam notes.,use one visualisation daily for a week and note what it taught,keep building new ones,synthesis,82,78,82,88,90,explore,Resolved true if fewer than 3 notes between 2026-10-02 and 2026-10-31 cite a site visualisation as the source of a finding; false if 3 or more do.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-031,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Am I moving myself out of the loop faster than I can verify what ships?,Most site PRs merge with agent-written evidence; no browser checks by policy.,personally review one shipped visualisation per day,trust the pipeline,synthesis,80,80,78,90,88,exploit,Resolved true if a user-visible defect in a shipped visualisation is reported in a commit or issue between 2026-10-02 and 2026-10-31 that the pipeline passed.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-055,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is my mathematics now spread across too many fields to make progress in any one?,"Motives, prisms, étale, Shimura, NCG, renormalisation, beams in two weeks.",pick one field for October,keep the breadth,synthesis,82,78,75,90,88,exploit,Resolved by a later note naming a single October focus and whether it held; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-044,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Are the site's WebMCP tools reaching any real agent today?,70 files register modelContext tools; no origin-trial token is deployed.,register an origin-trial token or stop adding tools,keep adding tools,synthesis,82,78,88,85,84,exploit,Resolved true if a later note or log shows a WebMCP tool call from a non-flagged browser; false if an audit finds none by the horizon.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-004,cal-2026-10-02-s1,"Has my note-taking dropped because agent-driven site work displaced it, rather than because I had less to note?","Notes commits: 9 on 26 Sep, 2 on 30 Sep, 0 on 1–2 Oct, while site commits peaked at 50.",block a daily 20-minute notes slot before any agent work,let notes follow whatever I am doing,synthesis,80,75,85,85,90,exploit,Resolved true if data/notes.md gains entries on at least 5 distinct days between 2026-10-03 and 2026-10-16 after a notes slot is adopted; unresolved if no slot is recorded.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-012,cal-2026-10-02-s1,"Will Groß score fewer points per match over Gameweeks 6–9 than his first five, enough to regret buying at peak?",He has 7 goal involvements on 2.63 xGI and is the most-bought player.,"skip Groß, buy an xGI-underperformer",buy Groß before the next price rise,synthesis,78,88,60,85,88,exploit,Resolved true if Groß averages under 5 points per appearance across Gameweeks 6–9 per the FPL API.,2026-11-08,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-033,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Do my crewmates currently hold a GitHub token that could delete a repository?,The PocketOS token was scoped for domains but could delete volumes.,"replace with fine-grained, no-delete tokens today",leave the token as is,synthesis,80,88,70,75,85,exploit,Resolved by a later note recording the token scopes checked; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-025,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is reading VGC guides now lower-value than building one team and laddering it for a week?,"My notes summarise Glick, Zheng and Traylor guides; none records a game.",build and ladder one team this week,finish the guide series first,synthesis,78,85,70,88,82,exploit,Resolved true if a VGC note dated by 2026-10-16 reports results from games played with a named team.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-032,cal-2026-10-02-s1,"Will I hit a hard-to-undo agent failure in the next three months, a leaked credential or a mass deletion?",A coding agent deleted a company's database with a token found in an unrelated file.,audit tokens and repo write scopes this week,rely on current guardrails,news,75,85,65,80,85,exploit,"Resolved true if a later note, commit or public report records a leaked credential or unrecoverable deletion caused by my agents before 2027-01-02.",2027-01-02,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-014,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Am I overweighting my own FPL data notes relative to simply copying the consensus wildcard template?,"Eleven FPL notes in three days; public guides converge on Saka, Arsenal defence, Groß, Haaland.",take the template and spend the time elsewhere,build my own differential squad,synthesis,75,80,80,85,82,explore,"Resolved true if a template-like squad would have outscored my actual squad over Gameweeks 6–10, per a later note; unresolved if not recorded.",2026-11-22,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-051,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Does the Lean formalization of Fermat's Last Theorem make formalizing my étale or Shimura notes in Lean worth two hours this month?,Claude agents produced 13 million Lean lines on Mathlib and Buzzard's project.,formalize one étale-cohomology note in Lean,keep notes informal,news,80,75,85,70,85,explore,Resolved true if a Lean file formalizing a statement from my notes is committed to a yujieteo repository by 2026-11-02.,2026-11-02,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-013,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is buying a below-xGI attacker such as Igor Thiago better than buying the in-form Groß for Gameweek 6?,"Thiago: 1 goal involvement on 3.29 xGI; Groß: 7 on 2.63.",buy the xGI underperformer,buy the form,notes,72,85,65,80,86,exploit,Resolved true if Igor Thiago outscores Groß over Gameweeks 6–9 per the FPL API.,2026-11-08,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-010,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Does the 'Wildcard' todo due 8 October actually mean my FPL wildcard chip?,The note gives no meaning; the FPL Gameweek 6 wildcard window closes 10 October.,decide the FPL wildcard today,treat it as an unrelated task,synthesis,75,85,90,50,85,exploit,Resolved by a later note naming what 'Wildcard' referred to; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-10,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-024,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Will I play at least 30 ranked Reg M-C games before 2 December?,Ten VGC notes this week but no recorded games.,set a 5-games-a-week floor,keep VGC as reading,synthesis,75,80,75,85,80,exploit,Resolved by a note recording games played in Reg M-C before 2026-12-02; unresolved if none.,2026-12-02,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-038,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Should I prune my skills repository rather than add more skills this month?,Seven new skills in five days; public skills are 92% flawed by one audit.,delete or merge the three least-used skills,keep adding skills,synthesis,75,75,75,88,84,exploit,Resolved true if yujieteo/skills has a commit removing or merging at least one skill by 2026-11-02.,2026-11-02,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-074,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is my working style now optimising speed before deciding direction?,"My note: sketch direction first; this week's output is mostly throughput.",write the direction in one paragraph before more shipping,keep shipping,synthesis,78,70,75,88,84,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note states a direction; then resolved true if it changes the work mix.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-016,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is Haaland at £15.6m a worse use of budget this month than two premium-priced cheap defenders and Saka?,2.5 points per million against Bogle's 9.1; 73.8% owned.,sell Haaland on the wildcard,keep Haaland for effective ownership,notes,70,85,55,88,84,exploit,"Resolved true if Haaland scores fewer points over Gameweeks 6–9 than the best-scoring alternative pairing priced within £15.6m, per a later note; unresolved otherwise.",2026-11-08,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-046,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is anyone other than me and my agents using teoyujie.org regularly?,No public analytics; repositories have 0 stars.,add privacy-preserving visit counts,keep building without audience data,project,80,70,80,80,82,explore,Resolved by a later note quoting visitor counts; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-021,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is FPL a better use of my analytical hours this month than VGC?,Both have about ten notes this week; FPL has a fixed weekly deadline.,cut VGC to zero hours until November,cut FPL to the weekly deadline only,synthesis,72,78,78,80,82,explore,Resolved by the share of FPL versus VGC notes between 2026-10-02 and 2026-10-31 together with a later note judging which paid off; unresolved without that note.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-063,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Would sharing beamdiag with one practising engineer give more information than another feature?,No external feedback is recorded for any engineering tool.,send it to one engineer this week,keep building,synthesis,80,75,78,70,78,explore,Resolved by a later note recording outside feedback on beamdiag; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-005,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Would two hours spent answering this Calibrator session beat two hours of more porting for what I do next week?,Calibrator went live today; raw.toon is empty.,finish at least the first 25 questions today,"answer later, keep shipping",calibration,70,80,70,60,90,exploit,Resolved true if data/calibrator/raw.toon contains this session with at least 25 answered questions by 2026-10-05.,2026-10-05,resolved,true,"raw.toon holds cal-2026-10-02-s1 with 100 answered questions, recorded on 2026-10-02 in https://github.com/yujieteo/site/commit/9b7bbc8a43280a8911a74b21e9dc42372688e557.","2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-006,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Will I still be answering a Calibrator session every week by mid-November?,First session; the spec names regular use as the bottleneck.,schedule a fixed weekly Calibrator slot now,use it when I feel like it,calibration,75,70,78,70,88,explore,Resolved true if raw.toon holds at least 5 sessions exported between 2026-10-02 and 2026-11-15.,2026-11-15,resolved,true,"raw.toon now holds five sessions exported between 2026-10-02 and 2026-11-15 (cal-2026-10-02-s1 to -s5, all exported on 2026-10-02), so the rule is met early; it says little about a weekly cadence.","2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-034,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is my no-mistakes review pipeline ceremony for most site changes rather than risk-dependent review?,My note says review effort should depend on risk; data-only PRs still run the full pipeline.,add a fast path for data-only and visual ports,keep one pipeline for all,notes,70,72,70,85,84,exploit,Resolved true if a risk-tiered review path is committed to a site playbook or firstmate configuration by 2026-11-02.,2026-11-02,resolved,true,"https://github.com/yujieteo/site/pull/125, merged 2026-10-02T06:48:08Z, adds the risk-tiered Review tier to skills/verify.md.","2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-061,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is structural engineering the domain where my tools have the clearest real users?,"Beamdiag, sectionlab, Mohr, stability, lug-joint, fastener-cg each have hand calculations.",invest in engineering tools and seek users,treat them as finished,synthesis,75,72,75,70,80,explore,Resolved by a later note recording external use or feedback of an engineering tool; unresolved otherwise.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-048,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is the notes-to-blog-deck-video-podcast pipeline worth its cost for each topic?,"One beam topic produced notes, post, deck, video and podcast on one day.",keep only notes and one derivative,keep the full pipeline,project,70,72,75,82,80,exploit,Resolved true if no topic after 2026-10-02 receives all five formats by 2026-11-30.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-045,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Should I stop adding WebMCP tools to new visualisations until the spec leaves the origin trial?,The trial runs to Chrome 156; Gemini support is still 'coming soon'.,stop adding WebMCP tools,keep WebMCP on every visual,news,70,72,75,80,80,exploit,Resolved true if no visualisation catalogued after 2026-10-03 registers WebMCP tools by 2026-11-30.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-073,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Would a six-month compression of my main ten-year goal change what I work on this week?,My note recommends the exercise; no goal is written down.,write the goal and the six-month plan,keep working opportunistically,notes,75,70,75,75,78,explore,Resolved by a later note recording the goal and whether weekly work changed; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-097,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Is my agent spend this month higher than what the site work is worth to me?,Opus 5.5 still prices output at $20 per million tokens; fleet runs daily.,set a monthly spend cap,keep spending,synthesis,70,70,70,85,78,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note records monthly spend and a value judgment.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
  cal-20261002-053,cal-2026-10-02-s1,Are my mathematics notes now better used as prompts for agents to verify than as things I compute myself?,My notes are 'mental computation' ladders; agents now prove large theorems.,have an agent check each ladder's claims,keep computing by hand,synthesis,75,60,80,80,82,explore,Resolved by a later note reporting an agent-check of a mental-computation ladder; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T03:40:00Z"
